    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "yeah, i checked for droppings but i honestly dont see much, it's just so hard to catch them. it's like they know exactly when i'm looking. \n\nand its not just the sound, things are actually moving. i'll organize a shelf of manuscripts, turn around to grab a lamp, and when i look back, one of the books is tilted or slightly out of place. it's like dozens of these tiny, little hands are just constantly adjusting things and causing minor chaos. it's so weird and almost feels... intentional? like they're trying to mess with the order of the archive. do you think there's any way it could be something other than just animals? like, could there be some kind of weird environmental reason for things to move like that in such a small, busy, scuttling way?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
