    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "it's hard to call it psychological when it's literally happening right in front of me. i saw a small, dark shape literally tugging at the corner of a page a second ago. it wasn't just a scurrying animal, it looked like it had purpose, like it was specifically trying to pry something open.\n\nit's honestly getting kind of creepy. it feels like this whole archive is being slowly, quietly undermined by these tiny, uninvited guests that just live in the cracks and shadows. it's like they're having a little party or something, just constantly nipping at the edges of everything while i'm trying to work. is there any folklore or even just common ways people describe these kinds of small, shadowy, mischievous little intruders that seem to thrive in old, dark places like this? i just want to know if there's a name for this kind of \"presence\" that messes with things.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
